# Seeker Project Rules

## Phase boundary

Phase 1 (current) is environment-only. Do NOT add game engine modules, game content, auth, or dashboards unless the task explicitly asks for Phase 2 work. Read `docs/VISION.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for product context.

## Stack (do not swap without instruction)

Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind at repo root, Prisma 6 + Postgres (Neon in prod, Docker Compose locally), Vitest, Playwright, GitHub Actions, pnpm.

## Quality gates

- Every change must pass `pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test` before it is considered done.
- Changes to pages or API routes must also pass `pnpm test:e2e` (requires local Postgres: `docker compose up -d`).
- Database schema changes go through Prisma migrations (`pnpm db:migrate`); never edit the database or migration history by hand.
- Never weaken, skip, or delete CI checks to make a failing build pass.

## Code style

- Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when interactivity requires it.
- Strong typing everywhere; no `any` unless unavoidable and commented.
- Small composable modules; shared logic lives in `lib/`.
- No secrets in the repo. `DATABASE_URL` comes from `.env` locally (gitignored), GitHub secrets in CI, Vercel env vars in deploys.

## When Phase 2 begins

Keep the three-layer boundary: `engine/` stays generic (no book-specific logic), `content/` is pure data (no business logic), platform concerns stay out of both.
